<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turku</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Åbo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Turku, Swedish Åbo, is a city on the south-west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> at the mouth of the Aura river. Founded in the thirteenth century around its cathedral and castle, it was the chief city of Finland under Swedish rule and the seat of its university from 1640. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> moved the capital to Helsinki in 1812, and a great fire in 1827 destroyed most of the old town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turku.jpg" alt="Turku" width="320" height="112" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Markus Koljonen (Dilaudid) with thanks to Jontts and Turku Cathedral · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_Turku_Cathedral_tower.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
